# Use cases > The map of it all
# ipm-overview:docs/use-cases/readme.md#L31
# ef1b92d59b7512ac69f84f6910bebca21635b2ee

# The root: using infinite.pm at all. Nothing is CONTAINED in it — the ways of
# using it are KINDS of it, so each one EXPRESSES it. That is also why there is
# no order here: different people take different paths, and most never take
# some of them at all. Order is a claim you can only make inside one journey.
all::a Use infinite.pm ::e

# One event per way of using it. Each is told in detail on its own page, where
# its steps are part of it and chained.
start::a Get started with infinite.pm ::e
edit::a Edit ipmt in VS Code ::e
preview::a Preview a standalone ipmt file ::e
render::a Render one diagram ::e
hand::a Refresh the diagrams by hand ::e
ci::a Take a change through the guard ::e
publish::a Publish a docs site ::e
site::a Read the website ::e
change::a Change the knowledge base ::e
mode::a Run the mode ::e
canvas::a Explore a graph in the canvas ::e
release::a Take a version through the release ::e
board::a Build a board of a corpus ::e
readboard::a Read a board ::e
union::a Build a union graph of a corpus ::e

start, edit, preview, render, hand, ci, publish, site, change, mode --::X--> all
canvas, board, readboard, union, release --::X--> all
